* Thu Aug 20 2026 Ackerman-00 <quietcraft@gmail.com> - 1.21.15b-0

- Fix OBS build: add BuildRequires mozilla-nspr to resolve the
  "have choice for libnspr4.so()(64bit)" error. The bundled NSPR libs
  make the package itself provide libnspr4/plc4/plds4, which conflicts
  with mozilla-nspr as the provider for mozilla-nss-certs' dependencies.

* Wed Aug 19 2026 GitHub Actions <actions@github.com> - 1.21.15b-0
- Update zen-browser to v1.21.15b

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Aug 19 19:06 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <quietcraft@gmail.com>

- Fix install failure on v1.21.15b: keep the bundled NSS stack.
  libxul.so references the NSS_3.126 versioned symbol which the system
  mozilla-nss (3.125) does not provide, so replacing the bundled NSS
  with system libs made zypper fail with "nothing provides
  libnss3.so(NSS_3.126)(64bit)". Ship the bundled NSS/NSPr libs and
  symlink only the root CA certs module (libnssckbi.so) from
  mozilla-nss-certs.

